      "diagnosis": {
        "cause": "KR-133 failed at “assert: a booking confirmation with a reference code is shown” because the submit handler only flashes a 2.5-second toast (“Done! Ref PL-4821”) and leaves the booking form on screen instead of rendering a persistent confirmation containing PL-4821.",
        "patterns": [
          "Ambiguous duplicate “Go” calls to action: the hero Go opens booking, while the header Go opens the hidden prices panel dead end.",
          "Blocking cookie overlay with a tiny unlabeled non-button close control (`div#cookie-close`).",
          "Form fields are identified only by placeholders; there are no associated visible `<label>` elements for name, email, or date.",
          "Date format requirements are undisclosed and validation reports only the generic message “Invalid input”.",
          "Arrival time and waiver controls are custom div-based controls instead of native radio/checkbox controls.",
          "Success feedback is transient: the PL-4821 reference appears only in a toast that is automatically hidden after 2.5 seconds."
        ],
        "filesToTouch": [
          "site/index.html"
        ],
        "changes": [
          "Add a persistent success element inside `section#booking`, after `form#booking-form`: e.g. `div#booking-confirmation.status[hidden][role=status][aria-live=polite][tabindex=-1]` with copy confirming the free first visit and a visible `Reference code: PL-4821`.",
          "Change the `form#booking-form` submit handler so a valid submission hides or disables the form, shows `#booking-confirmation`, scrolls/focuses it, and does not start any timer that removes PL-4821. The existing toast can be removed or left unused, but PL-4821 must remain in the page for at least five seconds and preferably persist until navigation.",
          "Replace the generic validation branch in the submit handler with specific messages, such as asking for name, email, YYYY-MM-DD date, arrival time, and waiver acceptance, and keep the error text in `p#error`.",
          "Add visible `<label for=\"name\">Your name</label>`, `<label for=\"email\">Email address</label>`, and `<label for=\"date\">Visit date</label>` around the existing inputs. Set useful attributes: `autocomplete`, `type=\"email\"` for email, and either `type=\"date\"` or a clear hint/placeholder saying `YYYY-MM-DD`.",
          "Replace the `div.times > div.time` arrival controls with a native radio group: a `fieldset`/`legend` for “Arrival time” and three labeled `input type=\"radio\" name=\"arrivalTime\"` options for 9am, 12pm, and 6pm. Keep the current visual button styling on the labels so the design remains the same.",
          "Replace `div#waiver.waiver` with a native labeled checkbox, e.g. `<label class=\"waiver\" for=\"waiver\"><input id=\"waiver\" name=\"waiver\" type=\"checkbox\" required> I accept the climbing waiver.</label>`, and update JavaScript to read `$('waiver').checked` instead of toggling a custom state.",
          "Make the cookie dismiss control a real, labelled button with a reasonable click target, e.g. `<button id=\"cookie-close\" class=\"cookie-close\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Dismiss cookie notice\">×</button>` or an “Accept and continue” button, while preserving the cookie-card styling.",
          "Rename both booking CTAs from ambiguous “Go” to an action such as “Book a free visit”. Update `button#nav-go` to call `openBooking()` instead of revealing `#prices`, so the header CTA does not lead to a dead end."
        ],
        "acceptanceCheck": "A fresh Kane run should be able to dismiss cookies, click a clearly labelled booking CTA, fill Sam Rivera / sam@example.com / 2026-11-02, choose the native 12pm arrival option, tick the native waiver checkbox, submit once, and immediately observe a persistent booking confirmation whose visible text includes the reference code PL-4821; PL-4821 must still be visible after a five-second wait.",
        "model": "gpt-5.5-2026-04-23",
